implementationPlan.description:
Tests first. Create moe-vscode/tests/seat-survival.test.cjs with the Write tool, modelled on tests/agent-seat-tracker.test.cjs (VSC-20, landed at 161c058c).

Harness: transpile src/util/SeatSurvival.ts with ts.transpileModule (CommonJS, ES2020). Run it through vm.runInThisContext('(function (exports, module, require) {...})') with a require that throws on every name. Returned objects then stay in the test realm, so strict deepEqual works (mem:gotcha-vscode-vm-test-harness). Every stub records its call first and only then acts; a stub that replaces the recorder makes its assertion vacuous. All assertions are exact-value.

Rows:
- S1, purity (DoD 1): the source text has no 'vscode' in any case (the same regex as P1 there), no import line and no 'require(' text. Object.keys(exports).sort() deep-equals ['SeatPids', 'isProcessAlive'].
- S2, isProcessAlive with a recording kill stub (DoD 2):
  - pid 4242 with a stub that returns gives true, and the stub log is exactly [[4242, 0]];
  - a stub that throws an error with code 'EPERM' gives true;
  - 'ESRCH' gives false; so do 'EINVAL', a thrown string and a thrown null;
  - 0, -1, 1.5, NaN, Infinity, Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER + 1, '42', undefined and null each give false with zero stub calls;
  - one real probe: isProcessAlive(process.pid) is true with the default kill.
- S3, SeatPids load (DoD 3), with a recording save:
  - load returning an array, a string, a number, null or undefined: seatOf finds nothing and save is never called;
  - a plain object {w1: 11, '  ': 12, w2: 0, w3: 1.5, w4: '13', w5: 14} keeps exactly w1 to 11 and w5 to 14 (seatOf(11) is 'w1', seatOf(14) is 'w5', seatOf(12) and seatOf(13) are undefined);
  - construction never calls save;
  - worker ids 'constructor' and 'hasOwnProperty' load and round-trip as plain data.
- S4, record:
  - a valid pair makes one save whose argument deep-equals the whole map; the same pair again makes no save;
  - an invalid pid (undefined, 0, -3, 2.5) or a blank or non-string worker id changes nothing and saves nothing;
  - a reused pid moves: record('w1', 11) then record('w2', 11) leaves seatOf(11) as 'w2', and the save no longer holds w1;
  - a worker re-recorded with a new pid drops its old pid: seatOf(old) is undefined;
  - two saves are never the same object, and mutating a saved object changes nothing inside SeatPids.
- S5, keep: keep(['w1']) drops every other worker, with exactly one save; a keep that drops nothing does not save; keep(undefined), keep('w1') and keep(null) keep none, with one save if anything was recorded.
- S6, surviving (DoD 4): with w1 to 11 (alive), w2 to 12 (dead) and w3 unrecorded:
  - surviving(['w2', 'w1', 'w3', 'w1'], isAlive) returns ['w1'];
  - isAlive is called only with 11 and 12: never for w3, never twice for w1;
  - a truthy result that is not true (1, 'yes') does not confirm;
  - a non-array (undefined, 'w1', {}) returns [] without calling isAlive.

Run `node --test moe-vscode/tests/seat-survival.test.cjs` in place (plain node, read-only; never npm in the shared checkout). It is RED, because the module does not exist yet.

Write moe-vscode/src/util/SeatSurvival.ts with the Write tool. No import, no 'require(' text, and no 'vscode' text in any case, comments included (say 'the editor's Terminal.processId'). Every dependency is a parameter, as in AgentSeatTracker.ts.

- Private isPid(value: unknown): value is number: typeof number, Number.isSafeInteger, and greater than 0.
- `export function isProcessAlive(pid: unknown, kill: (pid: number, signal: number) => unknown = (p, s) => process.kill(p, s)): boolean`:
  - return false before probing unless isPid(pid), because process.kill on 0 or a negative pid addresses process groups;
  - probe kill(pid, 0);
  - true when the probe returns, or throws an error whose code is 'EPERM' (the process exists but belongs to another user);
  - false on 'ESRCH' and on any other throw, non-objects included. Read the code as (err as { code?: unknown } | null)?.code; no any.
- `export class SeatPids`, holding a private Map<string, number> (never an object keyed by worker id):
  - constructor(load: () => unknown, save: (pids: Record<string, number>) => void) loads only from a plain object (non-null, not an array), applying record's rule entry by entry, without saving;
  - record(workerId: string, pid: number | undefined) ignores a non-string or blank worker id and an invalid pid. Otherwise it deletes any other worker that holds the pid, sets the pair, and saves only if the map changed;
  - keep(workerIds: unknown) drops every worker not in the array (a non-array keeps none) and saves only if something was dropped;
  - seatOf(pid) returns the worker id or undefined;
  - surviving(workerIds: unknown, isAlive: (pid: number) => boolean): string[] walks the array once, skips duplicates and ids without a recorded pid, and keeps an id only when isAlive(pid) === true;
  - save always receives Object.fromEntries(map), a fresh object.
- JSDoc on the module explains why it exists: terminals outlive a window reload and Restart Extensions, so VSC-21 marks the surviving seats launched() before the first connect. Each method gets its own JSDoc.

Error handling:
- Exceptions from load and save propagate unchanged; the callbacks VSC-21 injects own their catching, as in AgentSeatTracker.ts.
- isProcessAlive never throws.
- A recycled pid can make a dead seat look alive. That only delays its deregistration, which is the safe direction; record it as a note for VSC-21.

Re-run `node --test moe-vscode/tests/seat-survival.test.cjs`: every row passes.

Self-review of the diff, which is two new files only:
(1) purity holds: no import, no 'require(' text and no 'vscode' text;
(2) nothing throws except the injected callbacks;
(3) one worker per pid and one pid per worker hold after every operation, load included;
(4) save never fires without a change, and always receives a fresh object;
(5) prototype-named worker ids stay plain data (the Map);
(6) every DoD item has an exact-value assertion, and every recording stub records before acting;
(7) nothing outside the two files changed: AgentSeatTracker.ts, client-seat-tracker.json and extension.ts are untouched.
Put the findings in the step note, and fix any real defect before complete_task.
